        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"dumas-fils-la-dame-aux-camelias-30f4d3add98b26eb\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":3,\"performative\":3,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.92,\"analysis\":\"Marguerite’s conditional and hedged “je vous aimerai peut-être” presents possible future love as true while also functioning as a negotiated relational offer: Armand’s promised submission is made the condition of her prospective love and acceptance. The hedge prevents it from being an unqualified promise, but the surrounding language of terms and a signed “treaty” gives it substantial undertaking force. Nothing indicates that the words are a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The principal ambiguity is the balance between T and P: “peut-être” makes the future love a modal prospect rather than a firm commitment, while the if–then bargain and treaty framing nevertheless give the utterance significant performative force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Marguerite directly addresses Armand with a conditional, future-oriented equivalent of “I may/perhaps will love you.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Marguerite makes prospective love conditional on Armand promising unquestioning obedience, discretion, and respect for her freedom. The utterance is therefore both a hedged presentation of a possible future feeling and leverage in negotiating the terms of becoming lovers. Her subsequent description of their arrangement as a treaty reinforces this contractual framing. Although later bodily agitation suggests genuine emotional involvement may coexist with calculation, it does not make this utterance an expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“si vous me promettez de faire toutes mes volontés … je vous aimerai peut-être”\",\"supports\":\"The conditional construction presents possible future love and ties it to Armand’s undertaking, supporting both T and P.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Marguerite specifies that she wants a lover who is “confiant, soumis et discret,” while remaining free and giving no account of her life.\",\"supports\":\"The love utterance forms part of an explicit negotiation over the rights and obligations of their prospective relationship, strengthening P.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Marguerite says that “on ne peut pas toujours exécuter les traités le jour où on les signe.”\",\"supports\":\"Her own treaty metaphor retrospectively frames the exchange as establishing a relational arrangement rather than merely describing emotion.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The target contains the hedge “peut-être,” and Marguerite later answers Armand’s assurances with “Nous verrons.”\",\"supports\":\"The undertaking and prediction remain qualified rather than constituting an unconditional promise of love.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The supplied form metadata identifies the occurrence as affirmative future tense/aspect.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms the prospective rather than present-state orientation of the core utterance.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the hedged prospective avowal and conditional relational undertaking. The negotiation, possible calculation, and emotional undercurrent belong in contextual interpretation and create no residual core-force pressure.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
